### What is the three-way separation?

The locators live inside the page object, defined once as stable selectors. The interaction methods wrap actions into meaningful operations. The test logic calls these methods and makes assertions.

```typescript
// pages/TransferPage.ts - LOCATORS + INTERACTION
import { Page, Locator } from '@playwright/test';

export class TransferPage {
  readonly fromAccount: Locator;
  readonly toAccount: Locator;
  readonly amount: Locator;
  readonly transferButton: Locator;
  readonly successMessage: Locator;
  readonly errorMessage: Locator;

  constructor(private page: Page) {
    this.fromAccount = page.getByLabel('From Account');
    this.toAccount = page.getByLabel('To Account');
    this.amount = page.getByLabel('Amount');
    this.transferButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Transfer' });
    this.successMessage = page.getByText('Transfer Successful');
    this.errorMessage = page.getByRole('alert');
  }

  async navigate() { await this.page.goto('/transfer'); }

  async makeTransfer(from: string, to: string, amt: string) {
    await this.fromAccount.selectOption(from);
    await this.toAccount.fill(to);
    await this.amount.fill(amt);
    await this.transferButton.click();
  }
}
```

```typescript
// tests/transfer.spec.ts - TEST LOGIC
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';
import { TransferPage } from '../pages/TransferPage';

test('Successful transfer shows confirmation', async ({ page }) => {
  const transfer = new TransferPage(page);
  await transfer.navigate();
  await transfer.makeTransfer('Savings ACC-001', 'ACC-002', '5000');
  await expect(transfer.successMessage).toBeVisible();
});

test('Insufficient balance shows error', async ({ page }) => {
  const transfer = new TransferPage(page);
  await transfer.navigate();
  await transfer.makeTransfer('Savings ACC-001', 'ACC-002', '9999999');
  await expect(transfer.errorMessage).toContainText('Insufficient');
});
```

### What does POM buy you?

Three concrete benefits follow from the separation.

| Benefit | How It Works | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Reusability | Many tests call the same methods | Both tests above use makeTransfer |
| Maintainability | Changed locator fixed in one place | Rename 'Transfer' button -> edit TransferPage only |
| Readability | Specs read as user intent | "navigate, makeTransfer, expect success" |

### How do you avoid bloated page classes?

Decompose large pages into component objects. Shared parts like a header, search widget, or date picker become their own focused classes.

```typescript
// components/HeaderComponent.ts
import { Page, Locator } from '@playwright/test';

export class HeaderComponent {
  readonly accountName: Locator;
  readonly logoutButton: Locator;
  readonly notificationBell: Locator;

  constructor(page: Page) {
    this.accountName = page.getByTestId('header-account-name');
    this.logoutButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Logout' });
    this.notificationBell = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Notifications' });
  }

  async logout() { await this.logoutButton.click(); }
}

// pages/DashboardPage.ts - COMPOSES the header
export class DashboardPage {
  readonly header: HeaderComponent;
  readonly balanceCard: Locator;

  constructor(private page: Page) {
    this.header = new HeaderComponent(page);
    this.balanceCard = page.getByTestId('balance-card');
  }
}
```

### How do fixtures keep page objects clean?

Fixtures inject ready-to-use page objects and handle setup, keeping page objects focused purely on interaction.

```typescript
// fixtures/bankFixtures.ts
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test';
import { TransferPage } from '../pages/TransferPage';

export const test = base.extend<{ transferPage: TransferPage }>({
  transferPage: async ({ page }, use) => {
    const tp = new TransferPage(page);
    await tp.navigate();
    await use(tp);
  },
});
```

```typescript
// Spec uses the fixture: clean and focused
import { test, expect } from '../fixtures/bankFixtures';

test('Transfer via fixture', async ({ transferPage }) => {
  await transferPage.makeTransfer('Savings ACC-001', 'ACC-002', '5000');
  await expect(transferPage.successMessage).toBeVisible();
});
```

### Should assertions go inside page objects?

Keep business assertions in specs, not page objects. Page objects should be reusable by tests expecting different outcomes.

```typescript
// WRONG: assertion inside page object
async makeTransferAndExpectSuccess(from: string, to: string, amt: string) {
  await this.makeTransfer(from, to, amt);
  // This assertion does not belong here
  await expect(this.successMessage).toBeVisible();
}

// CORRECT: page object does interaction, spec does assertion
// Page: makeTransfer(from, to, amt)
// Spec: await expect(transfer.successMessage).toBeVisible();
// Spec: await expect(transfer.errorMessage).toContainText('Insufficient');
```

### How do you extract shared duplication?

Shared interaction logic gets extracted into component objects, utility helpers, or base classes.

```typescript
// Base page with common navigation
export class BasePage {
  readonly header: HeaderComponent;

  constructor(protected page: Page) {
    this.header = new HeaderComponent(page);
  }

  async waitForPageLoad() {
    await this.page.waitForLoadState('networkidle');
  }
}

// TransferPage extends BasePage
export class TransferPage extends BasePage {
  // Inherits header and waitForPageLoad
  constructor(page: Page) {
    super(page);
  }
}
```

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- "How deep should a page object's methods go?" Each method should represent one user action or a natural sequence. Do not make methods too granular or too coarse.
- "Can a page object return another page object?" Yes. A login method can return a DashboardPage, modeling the navigation flow.
- "What if a page is shared between two apps?" Extract the shared page object into a common package that both test suites import.

### What is the full example with all patterns?

A complete example showing specs, page objects, components, and fixtures working together.

```typescript
// Full example: spec -> fixture -> page object -> component
import { test, expect } from '../fixtures/bankFixtures';

test('Dashboard shows correct balance after transfer', async ({
  transferPage, dashboardPage, api
}) => {
  await api.seedAccount('ACC-001', 50000);
  await transferPage.navigate();
  await transferPage.makeTransfer('ACC-001', 'ACC-002', '5000');
  await expect(transferPage.successMessage).toBeVisible();

  await dashboardPage.navigate();
  await expect(dashboardPage.balanceCard).toContainText('45,000');
  await dashboardPage.header.logout();
});
```
